# Cloudflare static-asset headers (https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/static-assets/headers/).
# They apply only to files Cloudflare serves from the assets (this folder and
# Vite's /assets/), never to a response the Worker makes: the Worker's pages
# and endpoints set their own headers (src/start.ts). Every rule that matches
# a path applies, and a header two rules set is joined with a comma, so
# Cache-Control is set by one rule per path and never by /*.

# The headers src/lib/security-headers.ts gives the Worker's responses, minus
# the Content-Security-Policy, whose nonce is made per response.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=(), payment=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000; includeSubDomains

# Everything under /assets/ is built by Vite with a content hash in its name
# (the scripts, the stylesheet and the two fonts), so a changed file gets a new
# URL and an old one never changes: a return visit can use its copy without
# asking the network. Without this, Cloudflare answers with
# "max-age=0, must-revalidate", and Chromium revalidates a font on the first
# load of a new browser session, too late for font-display: optional to use it.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# The files of public/ keep their names across releases, so they get an hour,
# as the Node server gives them (SHORT_CACHE_CONTROL in src/node/static.ts),
# rather than a revalidation on every page load.
/lens-map.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/favicon.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/apple-touch-icon.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/og.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/icon-*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
